{
  "answer": "**Teatro Lírico Fluminense** (Teatro Lyrico Fluminense) in Rio de Janeiro. Gottschalk collapsed there during a concert in late November 1869, around the 24th. He died about three weeks later, on December 18, 1869.\n\nDependability varies across sources. Most say yellow fever, but one page says malaria. The cause of death is also disputed, with quinine overdose or sepsis suggested. The theater name is consistent across the sources, but I did not open the pages themselves, so this rests on the search summaries.\n\nSources:\n- [Louis Moreau Gottschalk – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk)\n- [Louis Moreau Gottschalk – Tamino Autographs](https://www.taminoautographs.com/blogs/autograph-blog/louis-moreau-gottschalk-the-first-great-american-composer)",
